(0) Print out the solved Exam.

(1) Look at the work shown for problem (1a) on the page on which the proble=
m occurs and also on the additional sheets.

(2) Count the number of additional sheets and take at least that many extra=
 sheets.

(3) Count the number of subparts for (1a) and list them in order.

(4) Start with the first such sub-part and complete your own calculation fo=
r that subpart in rough but without omitting any step and writing down all =
the steps that occur in the solved exam in complete detail.

(5) One should record one's work EXACTLY as in the solved exam in the same =
location of the sheet on which one wishes to record it MATHCHING EVERY SYMB=
OL AND ITS LOCATION WITH NO CHANGES, VARIATIONS, AND OMISSIONS.

(6) If one's writing is larger than the size that appears on the solved exa=
m, one may need more sheets.

(7) One mat NOT force-fit one'sr work into an inadequate amount of space by=
 putting strings of equalities on the same horizontal line because equaliti=
es and signs of equivalence MUST line up on the left.

(8) Repeat for every subpart of the work shown for problem (1a).

(9) If one's handwriting is larger than the handwriting on the solved exam,=
 one may record your work for each subpart IN ORDER from top to bottom sepa=
rating them with horizontal lines going across the sheet from one end to th=
e other end of the sheet parallel to the bottom edge.

(10) One must number the sheet on the lower right hand corner as in the sol=
ved exam and follow the numbering system if one needs additional pages.

(11) One must record one's answers on the page on which the problem occurs =
in case this is required, exactly as in the solved exam.

(12) One may NOT make ANY exrtraneous mark anywhere.

(13) One may NOT use ANY symbol that is NOT on the solved exam.

(14) Repeat with the remaining problems (1b), (2a), (2b), (3a), (3b).

(15) If one wishes to solve, (1c), (2c), or (3c) one must display one's wor=
k in a way similar to what one sees on the solved exam.

(14) FILL IN THE TOP SHEET CORRECTLY AS IN THE SOLVED EXAM.

(17) Use a ruler (or suitable software) to draw every line.

(18) Finish all work two days before it is due.

(19) Check all your work the day before it is due and submit.

(20) Check all details on the day of submission and make cosmetic changes i=
f necessary BEFORE THE DEADLINE.

(21) If you are careful from the beginning, there will NOT be any need to m=
ake cosmetic changes.

(22) Spend the day after the deadline on the following exam and start work =
on it IMMEDIATELY.

